{"slug":"ones-and-zeros-strings","title":"How Many Binary Strings Fit in the Budget?","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":735,"tags":["dp","knapsack","two-dimensional","strings"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"A knapsack with two capacities: a table over (zeros left, ones left)","body":["You have `k` strings made of `0` and `1`. You may take some of them, but the strings you take may contain **at most `m` zeros and at most `n` ones in total**. What is the largest number of strings you can take? For the strings `10 0001 111001 1 0` with `m = 5` and `n = 3` the answer is 4: take `10`, `0001`, `1` and `0` (5 zeros and 3 ones in total).","This is the 0/1 knapsack where every item has **two weights** (its zeros and its ones) and a value of 1. Let `best(i, j)` be the largest number of strings that fit into `i` zeros and `j` ones. For a string with `z` zeros and `o` ones: taking it is possible when `i >= z` and `j >= o`, and then the result is `best(i - z, j - o) + 1`. So **`best(i, j) = max(best(i, j), best(i - z, j - o) + 1)`**. Each string is used once, so the table is updated with **both indices going downwards**; then `best(i - z, j - o)` is still the value from before this string.",{"code":"best = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\nfor s in strs:\n    z = s.count(\"0\"); o = len(s) - z\n    for i in range(m, z - 1, -1):\n        for j in range(n, o - 1, -1):\n            best[i][j] = max(best[i][j], best[i - z][j - o] + 1)\nprint(best[m][n])"},"A knapsack with several limits just has a table with several dimensions. The time is O(k * m * n), about 2 million steps at the largest sizes, and the memory O(m * n). The answer is `best[m][n]`: since `best` never decreases with more room, the corner of the table holds the maximum."]},"statement":["`k` binary strings are given. Choose as many of them as possible so that the chosen strings contain in total at most `m` characters `0` and at most `n` characters `1`. Print the largest possible number of chosen strings."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `k`, `m` and `n`: the number of strings, the largest total number of zeros and the largest total number of ones.","Each of the next `k` lines has one string of `0` and `1` characters."],"outputFormat":["Print the largest number of strings."],"constraints":["1 <= k <= 300","0 <= m, n <= 80","1 <= length of each string <= 100"],"examples":[{"input":"5 5 3\n10\n0001\n111001\n1\n0\n","output":"4\n","note":"Take 10, 0001, 1 and 0: 5 zeros and 3 ones in total, 4 strings."},{"input":"3 1 1\n10\n0\n1\n","output":"2\n","note":"Take 0 and 1 (one zero, one one): 2 strings."}],"hints":["Each string has a number of zeros z and ones o and counts for 1 string.","Let best(i, j) be the largest number of strings that fit into i zeros and j ones.","Update best(i, j) = max(best(i, j), best(i - z, j - o) + 1) with i and j both going downwards."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nk, m, n = map(int, input().split())\nstrs = [input().strip() for _ in range(k)]\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long k;\n    long long m;\n    long long n;\n    cin >> k >> m >> n;\n    vector<string> strs(k);\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        cin >> strs[i];\n    }\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long k = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long m = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        String[] strs = new String[(int) k];\n        for (int i = 0; i < strs.length; i++) {\n            strs[i] = next();\n        }\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["A two-dimensional knapsack: best(i, j) is the largest number of strings that fit into i zeros and j ones; every string with z zeros and o ones updates the table with both indices going downwards, best(i, j) = max(best(i, j), best(i - z, j - o) + 1). The answer is best(m, n)."],"complexity":"Time O(k * m * n), space O(m * n).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nk, m, n = map(int, input().split())\nstrs = [input().strip() for _ in range(k)]\n\nbest = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\nfor s in strs:\n    z = s.count(\"0\")\n    o = len(s) - z\n    for i in range(m, z - 1, -1):\n        row = best[i]\n        prev = best[i - z]\n        for j in range(n, o - 1, -1):\n            if prev[j - o] + 1 > row[j]:\n                row[j] = prev[j - o] + 1\nprint(best[m][n])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long k;\n    long long m;\n    long long n;\n    cin >> k >> m >> n;\n    vector<string> strs(k);\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        cin >> strs[i];\n    }\n\n    vector<vector<int>> best(m + 1, vector<int>(n + 1, 0));\n    for (const string& s : strs) {\n        int z = (int)count(s.begin(), s.end(), '0');\n        int o = (int)s.size() - z;\n        for (int i = (int)m; i >= z; i--) {\n            for (int j = (int)n; j >= o; j--) {\n                best[i][j] = max(best[i][j], best[i - z][j - o] + 1);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    cout << best[m][n] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long k = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long m = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        String[] strs = new String[(int) k];\n        for (int i = 0; i < strs.length; i++) {\n            strs[i] = next();\n        }\n\n        int zeros = (int) m, ones = (int) n;\n        int[][] best = new int[zeros + 1][ones + 1];\n        for (int t = 0; t < k; t++) {\n            String s = strs[t];\n            int z = 0;\n            for (int p = 0; p < s.length(); p++) if (s.charAt(p) == '0') z++;\n            int o = s.length() - z;\n            for (int i = zeros; i >= z; i--) {\n                for (int j = ones; j >= o; j--) {\n                    best[i][j] = Math.max(best[i][j], best[i - z][j - o] + 1);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(best[zeros][ones]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"5 5 3\n10\n0001\n111001\n1\n0\n","output":"4\n"},{"input":"3 1 1\n10\n0\n1\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"1 0 0\n0\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"2 3 3\n1\n0\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"10 10 10\n000101\n00\n0110\n0\n01\n00\n00110\n0001\n0001\n1\n","output":"6\n"},{"input":"50 30 30\n001110\n00010\n0\n00111\n110\n10010\n0\n01001\n101111\n0\n11000110\n1000100\n1101001100\n1100100\n1000101\n0110001011\n111000\n1100111\n0\n0000010000\n10011\n1010101\n10\n001011\n0110001\n00000100\n1101110101\n1111\n10\n00111011\n1010000\n0001\n0000\n0011000\n0001001\n0\n001101\n110\n0101101000\n01\n0010010110\n111111\n111010101\n0101010\n0110101101\n1\n11110\n111\n1110\n10\n","output":"21\n"},{"input":"100 50 50\n11001111011001\n0110010001110\n00